<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan green coffee imports up 33.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan green coffee imports up 33.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in January totalled 27,431 tonnes, up 33.9 percent from the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 266 tonnes in January against 146 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Jan 97	   Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Total	   27,431	   23,959	   20,489</p>
<p> Indonesia	4,281	    4,506	    3,628</p>
<p> Colombia	 6,408	    5,380	    5,606</p>
<p> Brazil	   6,231	    7,837	    3,678</p>
<p> Guatemala	2,116		836		981</p>
<p> Honduras	 1,494		378		393</p>
<p>Total green coffee imports in 1996 were 326,388 tonnes, up 9.0 percent from 299,555 tonnes in the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Jan 97	  Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		266	     193		146</p>
<p>Cumulative roasted coffee imports in 1996 were 3,270 tonnes, up 57.6 percent from 2,075 tonnes the year before.</p>
</text>
